From 33d27229bf0a8e580cc77889c6d8159aab6a5ddc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 05:08:29 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] PS4: buffer checks skipped per 256 KiB word; changed uniform
 buffers copied, not uploaded; queued writes' repeats skipped

The skip gate's generation is kept per 256 KiB word and renewed only when a page in it goes
from clean to CPU-modified or untracked (04.86's per-4 MiB one was renewed by Breath of the
Wild's per-draw constant-buffer updates: 17% skipped). A cached uniform buffer found changed
by the CPU on consecutive binds is copied to the stream buffer for up to 7 binds, then uploaded
(an upload ends the render pass when the buffer is in use). The texture, query and shader
caches' sides of the queued writes' invalidation are skipped for a range they already ran on
with nothing new registered since. Uploads timed, render pass ends counted.
